---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — The Oracles"
  description="How The Oracles and its internal tool, Oracles Social, handle data, including Google user data."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="vhero">
    <h1 class="vhero__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="vhero__sub mono muted">Last updated: November 5, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="measure">
      <p class="lead">
        The Oracles (&ldquo;we&rdquo;) runs theoracles.studio and a small internal
        tool, Oracles Social, which reads performance numbers for The Oracles&rsquo;
        own social media accounts and can publish our own videos to them.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>What the tool accesses.</strong> When an Oracles team member signs
        in with Google, Oracles Social gets access to The Oracles&rsquo; YouTube
        channel and its data, such as video views, likes, comments and watch time.
        It may also upload The Oracles&rsquo; own videos to that channel when our
        team chooses to. It does not access any other user&rsquo;s or
        channel&rsquo;s data.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>How we use it.</strong> We use these numbers only to measure how
        our own videos perform. They are kept in our private records and are never
        sold, shared with third parties or used for advertising.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>Google user data.</strong> Our use of information received from
        Google APIs follows the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements. You can revoke the tool&rsquo;s
        access at any time at
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>This website.</strong> theoracles.studio does not require an
        account. If you email us, we use your message only to reply.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about this policy:
        <a href="mailto:hello@theoracles.studio">hello@theoracles.studio</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
